        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Consolidate automerge worker health",
        "body": "## What changed\n\n- removed the standalone Automerge Reliability sidebar panel\n- consolidated automerge repair workflow activity, stalls, failures, recoveries, and unresolved failures into Worker Health\n- kept PR and workflow run links while moving average runtime into secondary detail\n- labeled the data as Automerge worker operations so it is not confused with Automerge Product Health success metrics\n\n## Why\n\nAutomerge repair workflow reliability is an operational worker signal. Presenting it as a peer panel beside Worker Health made it too easy to confuse workflow failures with the separate product-level automerge success rate.\n\nThe workflow collection, cache, API payload, and hero attention signal remain unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pnpm run build:dashboard`\n- `node --test test/dashboard-worker.test.ts` (136 passed)\n- `pnpm run check`\n- autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings (`patch is correct`, confidence 0.93)\n\n",
